# WSL custom k6 (xk6)

Stock `apt` k6 has no Ansible Vault / faker / exec. Many perf repos need a custom binary.

**Build root:** prefer `paths.perf_tests` (perf repo), not qa-agent. Recipe uses `REPO_ROOT` so paths work on any machine.

## Prerequisites (inside WSL Ubuntu)

| Need | Check |
|------|--------|
| Go | `go version` (for `go install` xk6) |
| git | `git --version` |
| PATH | `~/go/bin` and `~/bin` on PATH (login shell) |

```bash
# PATH (add to ~/.bashrc if missing)
export PATH="$HOME/bin:$HOME/go/bin:$PATH"
```

## Recipe

```bash
# 0. Resolve repo root (path differs per user/machine)
# Prefer paths.perf_tests (WSL path of the perf repo)
REPO_ROOT="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || pwd)"
cd "$REPO_ROOT"

# 1. Install xk6 CLI
go install go.k6.io/xk6/cmd/xk6@latest

# 2. Build custom k6 binary
mkdir -p bin
~/go/bin/xk6 build v1.7.1 \
  --output "$REPO_ROOT/bin/k6-custom" \
  --with github.com/szkiba/xk6-ansible-vault@latest \
  --with github.com/grafana/xk6-faker@latest \
  --with github.com/grafana/xk6-exec@latest

# 3. Symlink to ~/bin/k6
mkdir -p ~/bin
[ -x ~/bin/k6 ] && mv ~/bin/k6 ~/bin/k6-old
ln -sf "$REPO_ROOT/bin/k6-custom" ~/bin/k6

# 4. Verify: must show exec + ansible-vault (and faker)
export PATH="$HOME/bin:$HOME/go/bin:$PATH"
k6 version
```

## Verify

- `command -v k6` > `$HOME/bin/k6` (symlink)
- `k6 version` output includes **exec** and **ansible-vault** (faker too)
- Pref: `tooling.k6_runner=wsl` when host k6 is blocked or you always run in WSL
- Pref: `tooling.k6_custom_wsl=true` after this build

## Installer shortcut (from qa-agent on Windows host)

```bash
node scripts/setup-wsl-tooling.js --install --only k6-custom
# optional: --repo "C:\path\to\your-perf-repo"
# stock apt only: --only k6
```

Onboard tooling **6** prefers this custom build (not stock apt alone).

## Do not

- Pin workshop `v0.43.1` (broken in 2026)
- Add `xk6-distributed-tracing` unless the team explicitly needs it
- Build into a directory named `k6` without `--output` (fails if `./k6` is a folder)
- Commit vault passwords or plaintext secrets

